---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'

const title = "When Base44 publish says success but live is unchanged"
const description = "Separate build failure, stale live output, and blank screens after publish on Base44."
const datePublished = "2026-09-02"
const url = 'https://base44expert.com/blog/base44-publish-error'

const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BlogPosting',
    headline: title,
    description,
    datePublished,
    author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Base44 Expert' },
    publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Base44 Expert', url: 'https://base44expert.com' },
    mainEntityOfPage: url,
    url,
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://base44expert.com/' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Blog', item: 'https://base44expert.com/blog' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: title, item: url },
    ],
  },
]
---

<Layout title={`${title} — Base44 Expert`} description={description} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <main id="main">
    <article class="section-padding">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <p class="label-eyebrow mb-2">
          <a href="/blog" class="underline underline-offset-2">Blog</a>
          <span aria-hidden="true"> · </span>
          <time datetime={datePublished}>{datePublished}</time>
        </p>
        <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl text-ink mb-8 text-balance">{title}</h1>
        <div class="prose-studio text-stone leading-relaxed space-y-4">
          <p>A common stuck moment: the UI says publish succeeded, but the live URL still shows yesterday’s version — or a blank screen.</p>
          <p>Treat these as different faults. A failed build needs logs. A “success” with stale live output may be caching, a wrong publish target, or a change that never left preview. A blank screen after an AI edit needs the last change and any console error you can copy.</p>
          <p>Check <a href="https://status.base44.com" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">platform status</a> first, then capture the exact message. We walk triage on <a href="/base44-not-working">/base44-not-working</a>.</p>
          <p>We do not invent incident queues. If you want a human pass, use <a href="/start">/start</a> with type <strong>publish</strong>.</p>

        </div>
        <p class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-line">
          <a href="/start" class="btn-primary">Start a diagnostic</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>
